      "title": "Fed chair says delivering ‘stable prices’ is central bank’s job as inflation persists",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/aug/28/kevin-warsh-federal-reserve-inflation",
      "description": "<p>However, Kevin Warsh didn’t say if interest rates would change in coming months, as inflation remains stubborn</p><p>The <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/federal-reserve\">US Federal Reserve</a> is not done fighting high inflation, its chair, Kevin Warsh, said in his first major speech in the role on Friday, emphasizing that it was “the Fed’s job to deliver stable prices”.</p><p>Warsh did not indicate where the Fed will take interest rates in the coming months, despite US inflation remaining stubbornly above the central bank’s 2% target amid the war in Iran. But his speech was taken by markets as a signal that rates may rise in the coming months, a move that may put him at odds with <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump\">Donald Trump</a>, who has aggressively called for rates to be cut.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/aug/28/kevin-warsh-federal-reserve-inflation\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-28T15:48:57"
    },
    {
      "title": "Kevin Warsh gets what every Fed chair hopes for: a bond market that trusts his word",
      "link": "https://www.marketwatch.com/story/kevin-warsh-gets-what-every-fed-chair-hopes-for-a-bond-market-that-trust-his-words-5103dad5?mod=mw_rss_topstories",
      "description": "Kevin Warsh passed another big test as a new Federal Reserve chairman on Friday: He said the central bank still has work to do on inflation, and the bond market took him at his word.",
      "source_name": "MarketWatch Top Stories",
      "published": "2026-08-28T20:10:00"
    }
